course: dictionary
lesson: 12462
title: Deficient: not having enough
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Deficient» means not having enough of something that is needed. Your body needs iron and vitamins to stay well. If it does not get enough, you are deficient in them. «Mia felt tired all the time because her diet was deficient in iron.»
explain: The word «not» is hidden inside the meaning. Check it by swapping in «did not have enough» and reading the sentence again. «The soil was deficient in nutrients, so the plants grew small and pale.» Swapped in, it reads «the soil did not have enough nutrients», and that still makes sense.
explain: «Deficient» can also mean not good enough. «His spelling was deficient, so he practised every night.» Here it means his spelling had weaknesses or faults. Look for the words after «deficient in» or «deficient», and ask: what is missing or weak?
fact: Deficient means not having enough of something that is needed.
fact: «Deficient in» is followed by the thing that is missing, such as «deficient in vitamin C».
fact: «Iron-deficient» and «vitamin-deficient» describe a body or a diet that lacks a needed mineral or vitamin.
fact: A diet deficient in vitamin C can cause illness.
fact: «Deficient» can also mean not good enough, with weaknesses or faults, as in «deficient skills».
exercise: «The plants grew pale because the soil was deficient in nutrients.» What does deficient mean here? | *Not having enough of something needed | Full to the top | Very colourful | Brand new
exercise: Which phrase tells you that a body lacks a needed vitamin or mineral? | *Iron-deficient | A tall, strong tree | A bright red coat | A fast, sunny day
exercise: «Her essay was deficient, with weak ideas and many spelling faults.» What does deficient suggest? | Finished early | Brilliant | *Not good enough, with weaknesses | Very long and very clever
test: «The children were deficient in vitamin D after a long, cloudy winter.» Which word means the same as deficient here? | Hungry | Bright | Crowded | *Lacking
test: Ben says «deficient» means full of energy. What is the correct meaning? | *Not having enough of something needed | Full of energy | Very fast | Bright and shiny
exam: A doctor says a patient is iron-deficient. What does this tell you? | The patient has too much iron | The patient is a famous scientist | The patient is very strong | *The patient does not have enough iron
